5:["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 sm:py-20","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-2","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mb-6","children":["About ","Scrivens Opticians & Hearing Care"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-base","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Scrivens is a well-established family-run opticians and hearing care group with around 100 branches across the Midlands, South West, and South of England. Founded in 1938, they combine the reach of a national chain with the personal touch of a family business. Scrivens is particularly well regarded for their hearing care services alongside traditional optical care, and they have been a trusted name in communities across their regions for decades."}],[["$","p","0",{"children":"Scrivens Opticians was founded in 1938 by Douglas Scrivens, who opened his first optical practice in the West Midlands. The business began modestly, offering eye tests and spectacles to the local community, but the quality of care and personal attention it provided quickly built a loyal customer base. Even during the difficult years of the Second World War, the practice continued to serve its patients, and by the post-war period, Douglas Scrivens had established a reputation that extended well beyond his immediate neighbourhood."}],["$","p","1",{"children":"The company expanded steadily through the second half of the twentieth century, opening new branches across the Midlands, the South West, and the South of England. In the 1980s, Scrivens made the strategic decision to add hearing care services to its optical practices, recognising the natural overlap between the two areas of sensory health. This dual-service model proved popular with patients, particularly older customers who could have both their eyes and hearing checked in a single visit. The hearing care division grew to become a significant part of the business, and today Scrivens is one of the largest independent providers of hearing aids in the UK."}],["$","p","2",{"children":"Scrivens remains a family-run business to this day, with the founding family maintaining an active role in the company. With around 100 branches, the group is large enough to invest in modern clinical equipment and professional training, yet small enough that individual branches retain a genuine sense of community. Scrivens is also one of the few optical groups in the UK to offer a comprehensive domiciliary (home visit) service, sending optometrists and audiologists to patients who are unable to travel to a branch. This service is particularly valued by elderly and housebound patients in the communities Scrivens serves."}]]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 h-fit","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-navy)] mb-4","children":"Quick Facts"}],["$","dl",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-sm","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex justify-between","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-gray-500","children":"Founded"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"font-medium text-[var(--color-navy)]","children":"1938"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex justify-between","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-gray-500","children":"UK Stores"}],"$L14"]}],"$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a"]}]]}]]}]}]
